commit 1c8039fe0d0b819ca010aeb0a2e02fff38ec9248

C03: an open order naming a near miss of a catalog application asks whether to open it (APPS1495)

«abres team», «Abre stea,», «Sí, abre Ste.», «abre Steel.» and «Sí. Abre Steel.» are transcription slips of Steam or Teams (the owner's notes: Steam was meant; use context or ask). No reader took them and the turn went to the model. `near_catalog_application_candidates` reads a plain open order («abres» joins the open heads) whose target is neither a catalog application nor an alias the catalog resolver authenticates, but is a prefix of three or more letters or one or two edits away from one or two catalog names (a short target such as «team» keeps both Teams and Steam); `_prepare_turn_result` answers it before resolving effects with `clarify_near_application`, one short question that asks whether to open the candidate(s), naming them exactly — validated (must name every candidate with an open verb, may not deny the application or claim not to understand) with one corrected retry — and opens nothing.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>


